package rsdl.showcase

// `Bench` (attributes.rsdl) places every instance of the closure once. `Road`
// breaks one placement rule per machine.
// RSDL-709 (rsdl reference §5): `slots` takes an integer from 1 to 65536. The
// error blocks `Road` only, which its placement errors already do.
deployment Road for Showcase [ slots = 0 ] {
  machine Ecu { Lane, Chassis, Brakes, Front, Hooter.left, Fleet, Siren, Dash }
  // RSDL-705 (rsdl reference §3.5): a second machine named `Ecu` in `Road`.
  // RSDL-706 (§9): `Hooter` places `Hooter.left` a second time.
  machine Ecu { Hooter }
  // RSDL-707 (§9): an external machine hosts external components only.
  machine Cloud [ external ] { Driver }
  // RSDL-702 (§9): `Draft` (attributes.rsdl) is outside the closure.
  machine Spare { Draft }
  // RSDL-701 (§9): `Rear.Unit` is placed on no machine of `Road`.
}

// The consumer links of `rsdl.showcase.alerts` in `Bench` (attributes.rsdl).
// RSDL-805, a warning (§5): `Dash [ depth = 2 ]` is below the contract bound
// 10 of `Alerts.honked`; the declared value is the link's depth for the
// half-open `Alerts.released` too, so `Dash` draws no RSDL-806.
// RSDL-806, a warning (§5): `Driver` (resolution.rsdl) declares no `depth`,
// and the depth of its link to the half-open `Alerts.released` cannot be
// derived; its link to `Alerts.honked` takes the contract bound and draws
// nothing. `Road` places both too, but an RSDL-7xx error blocks it (§13).
component Siren { offers rsdl.showcase.alerts }
component Dash { requires Alerts }

// RSDL-704 (§3.4): `Nowhere` names no declared system.
deployment Lab for Nowhere {}

// RSDL-708 (§3.4): a second deployment named `Bench`. It is `for` the second
// system (closure.rsdl), so it is not placed.
deployment Bench for Second {}
